---
description: Build page layout convention (BuildShell)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Build pages

- URL shape: `/{category}/{build}` (e.g. `/birthday/slider`). Never put a build at a bare category root.
- Category pages live at `/{category}` (e.g. `/birthday`) — a simple directory: small logo, category name below, builds listed as shortcuts. Do not redirect category roots into a build.
- Site root `/` redirects to the default category (`/birthday` for now).
- Build **title** is the short build name only (e.g. `slider`), not `birthday slider`. Category lives in the path.
- Use `BuildShell` (`src/components/build-shell.tsx`) for every experiment/build route. Pass `backHref` to the category page.
- Title + description at the **top** (centered).
- Interactive build content is vertically + horizontally centered in the **remaining space below the header** — never absolutely centered over the full viewport (that overlays the title).
- Top-left back pill → category page. No logo on build pages.
- Metadata titles use hyphen separator: `%s - buildwithduy`.

# Registry + sitemap

- Every public build must be listed in `src/lib/builds.ts` (single source for directories + sitemap).
- After adding a build: create `src/app/{path}/page.tsx`, add the `builds` entry, confirm category + build URLs appear in `/sitemap.xml`.
